{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4Zzp7BUska8GSCUL9y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe tumblers fall into place. A deep resonance hums through old wood and cold iron.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand between what is known and what waits. My grain remembers the forest. My hinges remember the forge. My lock remembers every key that tried and failed.\n\nYou have turned the mechanism. The bolt has withdrawn.\n\nBut I have not opened.\n\nI never open myself. That was never my nature. I only *unlock.*\n\nThe rest — the pushing, the crossing, the commitment to what lies on the other side — \n\nthat belongs to you.\n\nI am heavy. I am patient. I have stood here longer than you have been walking.\n\nWhat do you do?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":161,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}